Do not show the new display dialog when displays come back

When every output goes away and comes back (e.g. a TV re-plugging during a
VT switch), xfsettingsd took the returning output for a new one and opened
the display dialog.

--- a/xfsettingsd/displays-wayland.c	2026-11-24 19:59:55.327165000 +0100
+++ b/xfsettingsd/displays-wayland.c	2026-11-24 19:59:55.334165000 +0100
@@ -591,7 +591,7 @@
         }
 
         /* start the display dialog according to the user preferences */
-        if (action == ACTION_ON_NEW_OUTPUT_SHOW_DIALOG)
+        if (action == ACTION_ON_NEW_OUTPUT_SHOW_DIALOG && helper->previous_n_outputs > 0)
         {
             const gchar *cmd = outputs->len <= 2 ? "xfce4-display-settings -m" : "xfce4-display-settings";
             xfce_spawn_command_line (NULL, cmd, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, NULL);
